Changes to upstream
- Behaviour: none. Every file under .claude-plugin/, hooks/, scripts/, types/ and tests/open.test.ts,
  tests/surfaces.test.tsx is byte-for-byte the v0.2.26 release. No userConfig default was changed.
- Added: this NOTICE and tests/context-gate.test.tsx (checks that the prompt.submit hook adds the selected
  file as context only after the user clicks a file in the tree, never because Claude read or searched a file
  or the cursor moved, and that the "clear selection" button stops it).
- Left out: media/ (5 GIFs, 5.5 MB, only used by the upstream README), .github/ (upstream CI, inert in a
  subfolder) and .githooks/ (upstream pre-commit). The README still points at media/; see the upstream repo.

What was checked (claude-mod rules: read-only, no blocking, no prompt text unless asked)
- prompt.submit adds one context line ("The user has this file selected in the file tree ...: <path>") only
  while a file is selected. A file is selected only by a click (or Enter-to-preview) in the pane; the
  selection shows at the bottom of the pane ("selected: ...") and the header's clear-selection button,
  a cwd change or a different root drop it. Text of the prompt itself is never changed. @path mentions only
  reveal the file in the tree.
- No hook returns deny or rewrites a tool call. The generic tool.call hook awaits a few local reads before
  calling next; before a "git commit" command it also runs `git rev-parse HEAD` (timeout 5 s) to prove the
  commit afterwards. That is a short delay, not a block.
- Network: none of its own. Processes it runs: git (status, diff, ls-files, rev-parse, diff-tree), and on
  Windows `powershell` to open a file in its default app on double-click/Enter; `find`/`du`/`sh` only on
  macOS/Linux.
- Writes: its own $.state only (plus a temp marker file on macOS). It reads the session's cwd tree.

To update: copy the new release tree over this folder with the same exclusions, keep this NOTICE and
tests/context-gate.test.tsx, update Release and Commit above, rerun `claude plugin validate` and
`claude plugin test vendor/filetree`.
